DEFINITION OF DONE (DoD) - DESCRIPTIONS
=======================================


ARCHITECTURE AND TECHNOLOGY
---------------------------

[ ] Update existing module flow/flow diagrams. If none exist, create module
    flow/flow diagrams.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Team understanding/alignment is given.
    Description: Not specified.


CODE COMPLETE
-------------

[ ] Code is based on agreed design.
    Description:
    - For existing features that are expanded, design documentation is
      sometimes unavailable and creating it can require significant effort.
    - Short term: this criterion is valid for new features.
    - Long term: clarify whether all features require a design document and
      when investing the time is appropriate.

[ ] Push has a meaningful description and the work item ID is added.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Do reasonable functional testing.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Unit tests are performed successfully and cover at least 80%.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Checklist in Pull Request is filled.
    Description: See the "Checklist PR" section.


TEST COMPLETE
-------------

[ ] PBI is deployed to the PX environment and works as intended.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] PBI is at least tested manually on the demosystem. For "Feature complete",
    automated UI tests have to be done.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] All tests are successfully executed and test results are documented in the
    corresponding PBI.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Polarion test cases are written and linked. Each case should have at least
    1 good and 2 bad tests.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] All potential production-preventing issues must be fixed.
    Description: Not specified.


SECURITY
--------

[ ] State-of-the-art security technology must be used.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Communication outside of secured boundaries must be encrypted.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Secure boundaries must be respected.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Code must not be injectable (e.g. SQL injection, XSS).
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Third-party software which has critical issues must not be released.
    Description: Not specified.


DOCUMENTATION
-------------

[ ] Requirements are documented in Polarion.
    Description: A historical review note below says "specified" should be
    used instead of "documented" for REQ. This wording requires confirmation.

[ ] Technical documentation is created when the PBI is fully finished.
    Description: Historical review notes below say this criterion is not
    precise and needs clarification.

[ ] Documentation is reviewed and approved by at least one additional team
    member.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] Documentation is versioned.
    Description: Not specified.


CHECKLIST PR
------------

[ ] The changelog meets the defined quality criteria.
    Reference:
    https://uhlmann-group.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/W3/pages/801407460/Changelog

[ ] Inline documentation follows the development guidelines.
    Reference:
    https://uhlmann-group.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/W3/pages/801420391/Pexcite+Software+Development+Guidelines

[ ] Personal data is only persisted when it is strictly necessary and the
    purpose of any collected personal data is clearly documented.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] All user inputs are properly validated.
    Description: Not specified.

[ ] The source code contains no personally identifiable information.
    Description: Not specified.


